import std.dl

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] CPU vector
        vector
    members:
        x, y, z

a GPU vector means: @intrinsic("vector", 3)
the vector type means: a GPU vector if the build target is GPU, else a CPU vector
a new vector with x {a value:horizontal}, y {a value:vertical} and z {a value:depth} means: @intrinsic("construct", the vector type, horizontal, vertical, depth)
to get {vector:left} + right:
    set horizontal to ((the x of left) + right)
    set vertical to ((the y of left) + right)
    set depth to ((the z of left) + right)
    return a new vector with x horizontal, y vertical and z depth

to get {vector:left} * factor:
    set horizontal to ((the x of left) * factor)
    set vertical to ((the y of left) * factor)
    set depth to ((the z of left) * factor)
    return a new vector with x horizontal, y vertical and z depth

to get the string form of {vector:value}:
    set result to the string form of "["
    set separator to the string form of ", "
    add the string form of the x of value to result
    add separator to result
    add the string form of the y of value to result
    add separator to result
    add the string form of the z of value to result
    add the string form of "]" to result
    return result
